-- Generated: remove miscategorised routine-maintenance entries from transmissions.cons / transmissions.common_faults.
-- Scope: only entries classified A (bare maintenance-interval restatement), C-advice (generic
-- buying-advice like "check full service history"), and C-neglected-no-consequence ("often
-- neglected" with no stated damage) — see the A/B/C report for the full rationale.
-- Explicitly NOT touched: B (real neglect-causes-damage fault patterns), C-cost, C-access,
-- C-lifetime-claim entries — those stay exactly as they are.
-- Uses array_remove(), which removes every occurrence of the exact string from the array —
-- safe here since each removed string is the literal existing array element, not a substring.
-- Review before running. NOT executed against Supabase.

